# Landscape pipeline: the Python/analysis SOURCE stays tracked; only the
# generated artefacts are ignored. landscape/out holds jobs.json files of
# base64 genomes (~52 MB each) plus probe results — all regenerable from a
# run's genome.csv via landscape/stage{2,3,4,6}_*.py ... jobs, so they are
# scratch/HPC data, not repo data.
/landscape/out/ 
landscape/__pycache__/
*.zip.

# Per-seed map caches are regenerable from the seed (node generate_map_pool.js
# --seed N); the seed is the reproducible artifact, so don't bloat the repo with
# them. The active map_pool.json stays tracked.
src/maps/map_pool_seed*.json 

# Founder-genome probe units (jobs.json carries every genome as base64; ~330 MB
# per environment). Regenerate with assimilation/make_founder_jobs.py.
assimilation/out/

